    {
      "mechanism": "detector `port-binding-report` -- RD-02, and it was a detector that could not run",
      "reason": "ITS ENTRY POINT STOPPED ACCEPTING ITS OWN ARGV WHEN SM-02 LANDED, AND NOTHING\nNOTICED FOR TWO EPICS. The column passed `--port-manifest` to\n`run_generated_case_adapters.py`; SM-02 deleted that flag with the rest of the\n`[ports.*]` machinery. Since then the detector exits 2 with `unrecognized\narguments`, executes nothing, and the runner reports `INERT` -- which decides\nnothing and is correctly not a survival, so the table was never WRONG. It was\ncarrying a column that could never say anything again, in a file whose whole\nargument is that a control which cannot fail is worse than no control (R2).\n\nMeasured, not asserted. At `7514df0`, `SM-GM-P2` against this column:\n`INERT`, `executed = 0`, `exit = 2`, while `pytest-full` killed the same mutant\nat 1426 executed nodes. The gap this removal opens is therefore the gap the\ncolumn was already failing to cover, and `pytest-full` covers it -- re-measured\nafter the cut in\n`specs/results/scorecards/reading-discipline/GOAL-apparatus-priced/`.\n\nNamed here rather than deleted silently, because a detector that vanishes from\na table is how a denominator shrinks (`denominator_rule`).\n",
      "removed_by": "RD-02"
    },
    {
      "mechanism": "scripts/code_complexity.py -- the produced-code descriptor",
      "reason": "IT CORRECTLY CANNOT FAIL. It is a thermometer: it reports, refuses nothing,\ngates nothing, and `EXIT_OK = 0` is the only exit constant in the file. There is\nno gap to seed because there is no claim to catch anything. Named here so that\nits absence from the mutant table is a decision on the record rather than an\nomission, and so that SM-03 does not cut it by counting it with the other eight\nthat cannot be shown to fail.\n",
      "removed_by": "nothing; it is NOT a removal target"
    },
    {
      "mechanism": "registry row `test-graph-nodes` (test_graph/sources/)",
      "reason": "NOT IN THIS ENVIRONMENT. Running the Test Graph nodes needs gradle, a JVM and\nJBang, none of which are available here. A mutant seeded into them would report\nINERT on every detector, and an INERT row would be indistinguishable from a\nsurvival to any reader skimming the table. Declared unmeasured rather than\nmeasured as nothing.\n",
      "removed_by": "SM-03"
    },
    {
      "mechanism": "the `fake =` key of a `[ports.*]` table itself",
      "reason": "THE FAULT WOULD LIVE IN THE MECHANISM'S OWN DECLARATION. Dropping `fake =` from\n`case_adapters.port-swap.toml` is caught today by `render_oracle_statement`\n('is bound as a port and declares no fake'). But the table is deleted with the\nmachinery, so there is no post-removal tree the mutant could be re-applied to,\nand a before-only reading decides nothing about the cut. SM-GM-P2 seeds the\nequivalent drift in the MANIFEST instead, which outlives SM-02 and is therefore\nre-runnable. Reported so the difference is a decision, not an oversight.\n",
      "removed_by": "SM-02"
    },
    {
      "mechanism": "registry row `ticket-state-agreement`",
      "reason": "THE GAP IS ALREADY TOTAL AND THERE IS NOWHERE TO SEED IT. The row is classified\n`no-instrument-exists`: `ticket.yaml`'s `status` is written once by the\nscaffolder and read by nothing (`PA-02-DF-02`, open). Every `ticket.yaml` in the\ntree is under `specs/.history`, which is append-only and must not be mutated\neven in a copy. The cost of removing this row is therefore already paid in full\nand no mutant is needed to price it -- but it is named, because a row that\nvanishes silently from a removal table is how a denominator shrinks.\n",
      "removed_by": "SM-03"
    }
  ],
